Source: cares-rs
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Valentin Dudouyt <valentin.dudouyt@gmail.com>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cargo,
 rustc,
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libcares-rs2
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: libc-ares2 (= 1.34.6)
Conflicts: libc-ares2
Replaces: libc-ares2
Description: asynchronous DNS resolver library (Rust, c-ares-compatible) - runtime
 cares-rs is a Rust reimplementation of the c-ares asynchronous DNS resolver
 library, exposing the c-ares 1.34 C ABI under the stock c-ares names, so
 existing consumers link with -lcares and include <ares.h> unchanged.
 .
 This package contains the shared library (libcares.so.2) and replaces the
 stock c-ares runtime package.

Package: libcares-rs-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends: libcares-rs2 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Provides: libc-ares-dev (= 1.34.6)
Conflicts: libc-ares-dev
Replaces: libc-ares-dev
Description: asynchronous DNS resolver library (Rust, c-ares-compatible) - development
 cares-rs is a Rust reimplementation of the c-ares asynchronous DNS resolver
 library, exposing the c-ares 1.34 C ABI under the stock c-ares names, so
 existing consumers link with -lcares and include <ares.h> unchanged.
 .
 This package contains the development files: the C header (<ares.h>), the
 pkg-config metadata (libcares.pc), the CMake package configuration
 (c-ares-config.cmake), and the .so development symlink.
